WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.048
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online TOEIC preparation.

2
00:00:05.348 --> 00:00:08.955
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.255 --> 00:00:17.225
Unit eleven: Part 5: Parts of Speech. Today you will choose the correct word form: noun, verb, adjective or adverb.

4
00:00:17.525 --> 00:00:20.328
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:21.267 --> 00:00:24.465
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:25.317 --> 00:00:26.283
Noun.

7
00:00:27.283 --> 00:00:30.014
Noun means a word for a person, place or thing.

8
00:00:30.617 --> 00:00:32.024
Decision is a noun.

9
00:00:32.617 --> 00:00:34.967
Your turn. Say: Noun.

10
00:00:37.833 --> 00:00:38.765
Noun.

11
00:00:39.517 --> 00:00:40.274
Verb.

12
00:00:41.283 --> 00:00:43.794
Verb means a word for an action or state.

13
00:00:44.383 --> 00:00:45.802
Decide is a verb.

14
00:00:46.417 --> 00:00:48.732
Your turn. Say: Verb.

15
00:00:51.567 --> 00:00:52.173
Verb.

16
00:00:52.917 --> 00:00:53.848
Adjective.

17
00:00:54.850 --> 00:00:57.372
Adjective means a word that describes a noun.

18
00:00:57.983 --> 00:00:59.786
Decisive is an adjective.

19
00:01:00.383 --> 00:01:02.896
Your turn. Say: Adjective.

20
00:01:05.733 --> 00:01:06.665
Adjective.

21
00:01:07.417 --> 00:01:08.232
Adverb.

22
00:01:09.217 --> 00:01:12.238
Adverb means a word that describes a verb or adjective.

23
00:01:12.850 --> 00:01:14.722
Decisively is an adverb.

24
00:01:15.317 --> 00:01:17.528
Your turn. Say: Adverb.

25
00:01:20.367 --> 00:01:21.286
Adverb.

26
00:01:22.050 --> 00:01:23.179
Suffix.

27
00:01:24.183 --> 00:01:26.891
Suffix means letters added to the end of a word.

28
00:01:27.483 --> 00:01:29.367
The suffix -tion makes a noun.

29
00:01:29.983 --> 00:01:32.694
Your turn. Say: Suffix.

30
00:01:35.533 --> 00:01:36.662
Suffix.

31
00:01:37.417 --> 00:01:38.464
Word form.

32
00:01:39.450 --> 00:01:42.390
Word form means the shape of a word in a sentence.

33
00:01:42.983 --> 00:01:44.298
Check the word form.

34
00:01:44.883 --> 00:01:47.176
Your turn. Say: Word form.

35
00:01:50.033 --> 00:01:51.151
Word form.

36
00:01:51.917 --> 00:01:52.964
Modify.

37
00:01:53.950 --> 00:01:56.693
Modify means to describe or change the meaning.

38
00:01:57.283 --> 00:01:59.190
Adverbs modify verbs.

39
00:01:59.783 --> 00:02:02.540
Your turn. Say: Modify.

40
00:02:05.400 --> 00:02:06.424
Modify.

41
00:02:07.183 --> 00:02:08.359
Incomplete.

42
00:02:09.350 --> 00:02:11.350
Incomplete means not finished.

43
00:02:11.950 --> 00:02:14.321
Part 5 has incomplete sentences.

44
00:02:14.917 --> 00:02:17.325
Your turn. Say: Incomplete.

45
00:02:20.167 --> 00:02:21.319
Incomplete.

46
00:02:22.133 --> 00:02:25.575
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:26.417 --> 00:02:28.265
Visal, what is Part 5?

48
00:02:29.350 --> 00:02:40.318
It has thirty incomplete sentences. You choose the word or phrase that best completes each one. Many questions test grammar, and others test vocabulary.

49
00:02:41.417 --> 00:02:44.124
How do I answer word-form questions?

50
00:02:45.217 --> 00:03:00.622
Look at the gap and the words around it. After the, a noun or an adjective may come. After a verb, an adverb may modify it. A suffix can help: -tion and -ment often make nouns, -ly makes adverbs.

51
00:03:01.717 --> 00:03:03.159
How fast should I be?

52
00:03:04.250 --> 00:03:15.412
Aim for about twenty seconds per question. Grammar questions are often quick, so do not waste time and keep more minutes for long reading passages.

53
00:03:16.567 --> 00:03:18.113
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:18.950 --> 00:03:22.749
Grammar focus: Strategy: look at the words around the gap.

55
00:03:23.049 --> 00:03:24.201
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:24.917 --> 00:03:27.752
The manager made a quick decision about the budget (noun).

57
00:03:28.650 --> 00:03:31.172
She spoke clearly to the clients (adverb).

58
00:03:32.133 --> 00:03:38.954
Decide what part of speech the gap needs by looking at the words before and after it. Then choose the form with the right suffix.

59
00:03:39.717 --> 00:03:44.169
Be careful! Don't say: I choose a word without checking the position.

60
00:03:46.133 --> 00:03:48.864
Say: I check the words around the gap.

61
00:03:49.164 --> 00:03:50.386
Check the position.

62
00:03:51.200 --> 00:03:54.073
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

63
00:03:54.867 --> 00:03:56.239
Word Forms at Work.

64
00:03:56.539 --> 00:03:59.932
The sentence says: The company made a ___ about the new office.

65
00:04:00.933 --> 00:04:03.699
The gap comes after the article a and an adjective.

66
00:04:04.700 --> 00:04:06.688
So the missing word must be a noun.

67
00:04:07.700 --> 00:04:11.302
The options are decide, decision, decisive and decisively.

68
00:04:12.300 --> 00:04:13.951
Vuthy chooses decision.

69
00:04:15.067 --> 00:04:19.126
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

70
00:04:19.983 --> 00:04:21.751
Part 5 has blank questions.

71
00:04:22.051 --> 00:04:25.600
A, ten. B, one hundred. C, thirty.

72
00:04:29.133 --> 00:04:30.970
The answer is C: thirty.

73
00:04:32.117 --> 00:04:34.673
After the article 'a', the gap needs blank.

74
00:04:34.973 --> 00:04:40.252
A, a noun or adjective. B, a verb only. C, an adverb only.

75
00:04:43.800 --> 00:04:46.844
The answer is A: a noun or adjective.

76
00:04:47.983 --> 00:04:50.145
The suffix -ly often makes blank.

77
00:04:50.445 --> 00:04:54.018
A, a pronoun. B, an adverb. C, a noun.

78
00:04:57.567 --> 00:04:59.752
The answer is B: an adverb.

79
00:05:00.917 --> 00:05:03.357
Which word fits: made a blank?

80
00:05:03.657 --> 00:05:07.520
A, decide. B, decisively. C, decision.

81
00:05:11.067 --> 00:05:12.950
The answer is C: decision.

82
00:05:14.117 --> 00:05:16.279
How much time per Part 5 question?

83
00:05:16.579 --> 00:05:21.022
A, about twenty seconds. B, five minutes. C, one hour.

84
00:05:24.567 --> 00:05:27.402
The answer is A: about twenty seconds.

85
00:05:28.600 --> 00:05:32.030
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

86
00:05:32.883 --> 00:05:35.881
How do you choose the correct word form in Part 5?

87
00:05:44.683 --> 00:05:46.056
Now listen to Visal.

88
00:05:46.356 --> 00:05:58.194
I look at the words before and after the gap and decide the part of speech that fits. Then I choose the word with the correct suffix. I do this quickly so that I save time for Part 7.

89
00:05:58.494 --> 00:06:00.157
Excellent answer, Visal!

90
00:06:01.050 --> 00:06:06.349
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and strategy: look at the words around the gap.

91
00:06:06.649 --> 00:06:11.856
Today's value is precision of language. Choose your words carefully so others understand you.

92
00:06:12.156 --> 00:06:14.681
See you in Unit twelve. Goodbye!

93
00:06:14.981 --> 00:06:17.505
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

